te" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the third row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5359324fa248b36458bcfecab86ea4df13f93164aa03f4664aac764d91e33922" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" 