reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{33}$ and ${a}_{44}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/state.json" "file_sha256" "27e10012d1d1a627d933c4a3d173d6d504608ca6ed9c6b2c6e93313769fd808d" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-6166.json" "file_sha256" "ecc46975b9672648074bca266624acd2504115680e994b7e87e5e2a1e5e7835b" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-6166.json" "file_sha256" "ecc46975b9672648074bca266624acd2504115680e994b7e87e5e2a1e5e7835b" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4688.json" "file_sha256" "46b4c31b38985034dce44d993adf9c0dc1160b33e01959ca8a4bb0af86a7fd90" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 7 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4688.json" "file_sha256" "46b4c31b38985034dce44d993adf9c0dc1160b33e01959ca8a4bb0af86a7fd90" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4687.json" "file_sha256" "203c1e0fc35513780b3743d8832441145bc026f96e039c3efbe0407b9267a626" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4687.json" "file_sha256" "203c1e0fc35513780b3743d8832441145bc026f96e039c3efbe0407b9267a626" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4689.json" "file_sha256" "1ea65c09e1096e026a31ea18f39351049ec3554e2a128d76e81e8ad5b66c9af8" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/example-4689.json" "file_sha256" "1ea65c09e1096e026a31ea18f39351049ec3554e2a128d76e81e8ad5b66c9af8" "basis" 1392 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039880/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-73145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows of $A$ are $1$ and $-3$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+(-3)=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-73145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $1$ and $6$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+6=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-73146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows of $A$ are $-7$, $5$, and $3$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-7+5+3=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st and $3$rd rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st and $3$rd rows of $A$ are $4$ and $-1$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $4+(-1)=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-73143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-73143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows of  $A$ are $1$ and $3$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+3=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-129210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${a}_{43}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-72491" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/