" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$  is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-72570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-72570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$B$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the third row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-129232" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-42028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa05f8c056e95e2a6435d78375d3d8cf4b48e1270110dca7e56a0406ab180fd0"} {"question" "q-42006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf392549f95d0903"} {"question" "q-42006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7eec79cfad6a2a5967094f14d52db2086f21266b4a158eabf39254